course: dictionary
lesson: 10621
title: Unfaithful and broken promises
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Unfaithful means not loyal. Someone who breaks a promise, or lets down a person who trusted them, is unfaithful. You can find the meaning in the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble.» A broken tooth and a lame foot let you down when you need them most. So trusting an unfaithful person in trouble is like leaning on something that is broken.
explain: The start of the word gives a clue. Un- means not, and faithful means loyal and true to your promises, so unfaithful means not loyal. In grown-up life, a partner can be unfaithful when they break their promise to each other. That is a grown-up matter, and it is never a child's fault.
fact: Unfaithful means not loyal, breaking a promise or letting down someone who trusted you.
fact: A husband, wife or partner is unfaithful when they secretly start a love relationship with someone else, which breaks their promise to each other.
fact: In formal writing, an unfaithful copy or translation does not match the original exactly.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unfaithful is the opposite of faithful.
fact: «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble» (Proverbs 25:19) warns that trusting someone who lets you down hurts most when you need help.
exercise: Mia promised to help, but she never turned up. Mia was unfaithful. What does unfaithful mean? | Made of soft cloth | Very happy and full of energy | *Not loyal, letting down someone who trusted her
exercise: «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble.» What does unfaithful mean here? | A person who is always on time | *Someone who lets you down when you need them | A person who has a strong, healthy foot
exercise: What does an unfaithful translation mean? | *Does not match the original exactly | Is read aloud in a loud voice | Is written in gold ink | Is very short
test: Which word is the opposite of unfaithful? | *Faithful | Tired | Careless | Angry
test: When grown-ups are unfaithful to each other and split up, whose fault is it? | The neighbour's | Shared equally by all the children | The school's | *Never the child's; it is a grown-up matter
exam: In «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble», what are the broken tooth and lame foot like? | Things that make you laugh | Things you can keep forever | *Things that let you down when you need them | Things that glow in the dark
